Together the two functions separate the three cultivars much better than either function alone.

## Allocation rule and training error

The source classifies from LD1 alone using cut points -1.751107 and 2.122505.

```biolang
let classified = scored |> mutate("predicted", |row|
    if row.LD1 <= -1.751107 { 1 } else { if row.LD1 <= 2.122505 { 2 } else { 3 } })
let c11 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 1 && row.predicted == 1) |> nrow()
let c12 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 1 && row.predicted == 2) |> nrow()
let c13 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 1 && row.predicted == 3) |> nrow()
let c21 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 2 && row.predicted == 1) |> nrow()
let c22 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 2 && row.predicted == 2) |> nrow()
let c23 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 2 && row.predicted == 3) |> nrow()
let c31 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 3 && row.predicted == 1) |> nrow()
let c32 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 3 && row.predicted == 2) |> nrow()
let c33 = classified |> filter(|row| row.V1 == 3 && row.predicted == 3) |> nrow()
table({
    actual: ["cultivar 1", "cultivar 2", "cultivar 3"],
    predicted_1: [c11, c21, c31],
    predicted_2: [c12, c22, c32],
    predicted_3: [c13, c23, c33]
})
```

The exact confusion matrix is `[56,3,0]`, `[5,65,1]`, `[0,0,48]`: nine errors among 178 samples, or 5.1%. This is resubstitution performance on the training observations and is optimistic; the source explicitly makes the same warning.

```biolang
assert abs(ld1_groups[0] + 3.42248851) < 0.000001, "source cultivar 1 LD1 mean"
assert abs(ld1_groups[1] + 0.07972623) < 0.000001, "source cultivar 2 LD1 mean"
assert abs(ld1_groups[2] - 4.32473717) < 0.000001, "source cultivar 3 LD1 mean"
assert abs(ld2_groups[0] - 1.691674) < 0.000001 && abs(ld2_groups[1] + 2.472656) < 0.000001 && abs(ld2_groups[2] - 1.578120) < 0.000001, "source LD2 group means"
assert abs(ld1_separation - 794.6522) < 0.001, "source LD1 separation"
assert abs(ld2_separation - 361.2410) < 0.001, "source LD2 separation"
assert c11 == 56 && c12 == 3 && c13 == 0, "source cultivar 1 allocations"
assert c21 == 5 && c22 == 65 && c23 == 1, "source cultivar 2 allocations"
assert c31 == 0 && c32 == 0 && c33 == 48, "source cultivar 3 allocations"
"Published LDA coefficients, downstream scores, separation, allocation rule, and three canonical figures verified."
```

